\begin_layout Standard
Note that the baseline treatment is identified by the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

high earner / windfall money
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 cell.
 Subjects participating in the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

earned monies
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 treatment will receive their endowments based on how they perform on a
 set number of algebraic math problems.
 In all treatments, those subjects that have been given the allocation decision
 will have the ability to take funds from their partner.
 Partners will still be randomly determined, but the subjects wil be made
 aware if they are either a 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

high earner
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 or 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

low earner
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 relative to their partner.
 Will low earners exhibit a higher propensity to 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

take
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 from their high earning partner? Does this attitude change depending on
 if the money is earned or not?
\end_layout

